{"id":3781,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple/","parentId":540,"order":50,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Present simple: I do, I don’t, Do I?","seo":{"title":"Present simple: I do, I don't, Do I? - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use the present simple tense in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_Present-simple.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T09:27:26","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct present simple forms to complete the following sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"430\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Transform the following sentences into negatives.</h5> <p>&nbsp;<br> <em>EXAMPLE: I love pizza. ⇒ I <span class=\"textGap\">don’t love</span> pizza.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"431\"></div> <p></p>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write questions in present simple.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: Peter / drive / a fast car. ⇒ <span class=\"textGap\">Does Peter drive a fast car</span>?</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"432\"></div> <p></p>","<h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h5>Fill in the gaps with the verbs in brackets in present simple affirmative or negative.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"433\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Present simple form</h2> <p>In present simple verbs, we need to use the verb <strong>do/does</strong> in questions and <strong>don’t/doesn’t</strong> in negatives.<br> <br> <img src=\"/media/uploads/present-simple-form_a1.png\" alt=\"Grammar infographic showing the structure of the Present Simple tense in English, including positive forms, negative forms, questions, and short answers for A1 elementary learners.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-10944\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Spelling of <strong>he/she/it</strong></h4> <p>The form is the same for all the other persons except <strong>he/she/it</strong>. The spelling for&nbsp;<strong>he/she/it</strong>&nbsp;is different.<br> <br> <img src=\"/media/uploads/present-simple-spelling-he-she-it.png\" alt=\"Grammar chart demonstrating Present Simple tense spelling rules for third-person singular subjects (he, she, it) with examples of verb conjugations and common mistakes.\" width=\"500\" height=\"501\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-25842\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>Present simple use</h2> <h4>Habits or actions&nbsp;that happen regularly</h4> <p>We use present simple for habits or actions that we repeat regularly:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I&nbsp;<span><strong>wash</strong></span>&nbsp;my hair every day.</em></li> <li><em>I never&nbsp;<span><strong>go</strong></span>&nbsp;to the library.</em></li> <li><em>I&nbsp;<span><strong>go</strong></span>&nbsp;to the library on Saturdays.</em></li> </ul> <h4>Permanent situations or things that are always or often true</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I&nbsp;<span><strong>don’t drink</strong></span>&nbsp;coffee.</em></li> <li><em>She<span><strong>’s</strong></span>&nbsp;very tall.</em></li> <li><em>I&nbsp;<span><strong>have</strong></span>&nbsp;two brothers.</em></li> <li><em>Water&nbsp;<span><strong>boils</strong></span>&nbsp;at 100 degrees.</em></li> <li><em>I&nbsp;<span><strong>like</strong></span>&nbsp;soup.</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":430,"questions":[{"id":3728,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> tea.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["not drink","don't drink","drink not"]}]},{"id":3729,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> two brothers. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["haves","have","has"]}]},{"id":3730,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Tom <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> work until 10 today. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["doesn't start","do not start","doesn't starts"]}]},{"id":3731,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> an instrument?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["You play","Do you play","You do play"]}]},{"id":3732,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The museum <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> at 10 o'clock. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["does open","open","opens"]}]},{"id":3733,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Peter and Megan often <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to the cinema. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["go","do go","goes"]}]},{"id":3734,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>John <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> very late. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["doesn't gets up","do not get up","doesn't get up"]}]},{"id":3735,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What time <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> home in the morning?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["they do leave","do they leave","they leave"]}]},{"id":3736,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What language <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["does he studies","does he study","do he studies"]}]},{"id":3737,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My son never <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> cartoons.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["watches","watch","watchs"]}]}]},{"id":431,"questions":[{"id":3738,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He is a student. ⇒ He <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a student.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3739,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Peter works in an office. ⇒ Peter <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in an office.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3740,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My parents live in Arizona. ⇒ My parents <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in Arizona. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3741,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Suzan likes cats. ⇒ Suzan <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> cats. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3742,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He has brothers and sisters. ⇒ He <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> any brothers or sisters. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3743,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She speaks three languages. ⇒ She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> three languages. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3744,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>John and I want to be musicians. ⇒ John and I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to be musicians. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3745,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They play tennis. ⇒ They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> tennis.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3746,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She gets home late. ⇒ She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> home late. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3747,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Anna and Paul live in the center. ⇒ Anna and Paul <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in the center. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":432,"questions":[{"id":3748,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Laura / play / tennis ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3749,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>you / speak / English ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3750,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>you / want / some coffee ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3751,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Where / he / live ⇒ Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>? </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3752,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>How often / they / go to the cinema ⇒ How often <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3753,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What time / Suzan / start work ⇒ What time <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3754,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Where / she / work ⇒ Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3755,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>you / listen to music ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3756,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>he / watch / series ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3757,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>How often / they / travel ⇒ How often <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":433,"questions":[{"id":3758,"num":"","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p class=\"double-line-height\">Sara is my daughter. She <span class=\"textGap\">has</span> (have) two daughters; they are my granddaughters. Sara <span class=\"numBox\">1</span> <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (not have) much free time because she <span class=\"numBox\">2</span> <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> (work) in a shop. In the week, she <span class=\"numBox\">3</span> <span data-gap=\"2\"></span> (get up) very early and she <span class=\"numBox\">4</span> <span data-gap=\"3\"></span> (go) to bed quite late every day. She <span class=\"numBox\">5</span> <span data-gap=\"4\"></span> (love) Sundays because she <span class=\"numBox\">6</span> <span data-gap=\"5\"></span> (not work) and she <span class=\"numBox\">7</span> <span data-gap=\"6\"></span> (spend) the day with her family. On Sundays, they <span class=\"numBox\">8</span> <span data-gap=\"7\"></span> (not get up) very late because they always <span class=\"numBox\">9</span> <span data-gap=\"8\"></span> (go out). My granddaughters <span class=\"numBox\">10</span> <span data-gap=\"9\"></span> (be) always sad on Sunday evenings because it's the end of the weekend.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}